# 12. Technical production standards

A beautiful website that fails under real conditions is not FAANG-grade.

The following is the acceptance standard I recommend.

## A. SEO and domain integrity

The issues in your audit must be treated as release blockers.

| Area                | Required outcome                                        |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Production hostname | One verified canonical hostname                         |
| Navigation          | All links use the canonical origin                      |
| Canonical tags      | Self-referencing per indexable page                     |
| Open Graph          | Correct production URLs and images                      |
| Robots              | Deliberate, consistent indexation policy                |
| Sitemap             | Only canonical, indexable URLs                          |
| Robots.txt          | Matches intended indexing policy                        |
| Redirects           | Preview and obsolete aliases handled deliberately       |
| Metadata            | Unique page titles and descriptions                     |
| Structured data     | Only truthful Organization, WebSite and relevant schema |
| Social previews     | Valid image, title and description                      |

One important qualification: preview environments may legitimately be `noindex`. The production site should not inherit that setting accidentally. Do not blindly remove `noindex` from preview deployments.

The branch-preview hostname should never become the canonical production identity.

## B. Performance engineering

Set explicit budgets rather than just saying "fast."

Core Web Vitals targets

# LCP

# ≤2.5s

Largest Contentful Paint

# INP

# ≤200ms

Interaction to Next Paint

# CLS

# ≤0.1

Cumulative Layout Shift

These are Google's good Core Web Vitals thresholds, measured at the 75th percentile of real-user visits.

Additional budgets:

- Initial JavaScript: keep exceptionally small; target under 100 KB compressed where architecture permits.
- Initial CSS: target under 50 KB compressed.
- No unnecessary third-party scripts.
- Responsive AVIF/WebP imagery.
- Explicit image dimensions.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold images.
- Prioritize the actual hero asset.
- Self-host optimized fonts where practical.
- `font-display: swap`.
- Avoid loading multiple font weights unnecessarily.
- No layout shifts from late-loading content.

Don't treat these numbers as achieved results until measured.

## C. Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA.

Required:

- Semantic landmarks.
- Correct heading hierarchy.
- Skip link.
- Keyboard navigation.
- Visible focus indicators.
- Accessible form labels.
- Error identification and recovery.
- Appropriate live announcements.
- Color contrast.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Correct dialog/disclosure behavior.
- Screen-reader testing.

Specifically test the intake wizard using:

- Keyboard only.
- NVDA with Firefox.
- VoiceOver with Safari, where available.

Automated axe checks cannot replace manual testing.

## D. Security and privacy

- No exposed secrets.
- No personal WhatsApp number printed in the UI.
- No unnecessary tracking.
- No collection of project details without disclosure.
- Correct security headers.
- Safe link handling.
- Dependency auditing.
- Content Security Policy compatible with the actual site.
- No unsafe DOM insertion.
- No unnecessary client-side dependencies.

## E. Cross-browser verification

Test:

- Chrome.
- Firefox.
- Safari.
- Edge.
- Android Chrome.
- iOS Safari.

Test both touch and keyboard interaction.

## F. Automated CI gates

Every change should pass:

| Gate            | Requirement                                      |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| HTML validation | No material markup errors                        |
| Link checker    | No broken internal links                         |
| Unit tests      | All pass                                         |
| Browser tests   | Critical journeys pass                           |
| Accessibility   | No unresolved critical/serious violations        |
| SEO tests       | Metadata, canonicals, robots and sitemap correct |
| Performance     | Defined budgets respected                        |
| Security        | Dependency and configuration checks pass         |
| Build           | Reproducible production build                    |
| Deployment      | Live production smoke tests pass                 |

The site must not declare itself release-ready because the local build succeeded.

